Branch :
 It is a separate work space where developers can create new codes on which they want to do experiments
 Then they can merge entire data into main branch only so that we can avoid disturbing current main branch


 Now I was new one assigned for the project which was currently working then I have to made changes and updates if needed.
 so now i dont have to work on the main branch directly, if i do so the whole website would be blocked if i do any mistake
 so we can create a duplicate branch and work on the project through that duplicate branch and then we can merge that to the main branch after checking the working of our duplicate branch
 For doing that the following are the commands...........
 1)git branch                   -- check the branch (main branch)
 2)git branch practice          -- the duplicate branch that we want to work on
 3)git branch                   -- to check the status of duplicate branch and how many branches are exist till then
 4)git checkout practice        -- here these command allows us to switch to practice branch
 5)git branch                   -- now we can check that the curser was switched to duplicate branch or not(We can observe that change through the green color branch was currently switched branch)


 Now if add anything in the new duplicate branch then
 1)add that line in the duplicate branch
 2)git status - shows that something got added on practice/duplicate branch and not commited yet
 3)git commit -aM "new line added to duplicate branch" - It saves the new code on the replica branch
 4)git status - Here it shows that everything was fine in the replica branch
 5)git checkout main - Here curser switch to the main branch
 6)git branch - tells that the current branch main branch as an indication of green colour

 now if we want to merge or add our duplicate branch to the main branch then..........
 7)git merge practice - It merge or add our duplicate branch to the main branch

 --->To know about merge conflict :
 now if we add something in main branch and commit it and |switch to practice branch..........
 now without adding or merging the main branch new data if we also go to duplicate branch and add some code and then commit it |switch to main branch..........
 we can see that main branch only contains the new data added in the main branch and if we see the practice branch there is only practice branch new data was added
 now if we use (git merge practice)  for merging both main and practice branches
 then it shows us three options as if we can go with main branch changes / practice branch changes / both of their changes

 --->If we want to push our practice branch into github repository............
 git push -U origin practice - these command pushes our practice branch also to our project repository

 --->If we want to delete the practice branch...........
 git branch -d practice - these command allows us to delete the branch that we want to delete

